  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "14. Objectives",
    "ruleNumber": "14.02",
    "order": 188,
    "anchor": "14.02",
    "summary": "No player controls any **objective** when the battle begins. To control one, a player needs models with an OC of at least 1 in range of it; for a **terrain objective**, being inside its **terrain area** counts as in range.\n\nAs each phase and each turn ends, add up the OC values of all a player's models in range of each objective to get their **level of control** there:\n\n- The higher level controls it.\n- Equal levels leave it uncontrolled unless it is secured (14.03).\n\nA unit of the controlling player counts as controlling the objective while the unit is in range and has a model whose OC is at least 1.",
